{"content_hash": "ea1b64f2740ea4b4", "version_id": 97, "article_id": 10, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "NATOの近くでドローンが船を沈めた EUは「ゆるせない」と言った", "title_zh": "北约附近无人机击沉货船，欧盟说“无法接受”", "topic": "tech", "source": "arstechnica", "source_url": "https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/10/drone-strikes-likely-russian-sink-ships-in-nato-countries-economic-zones/", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.rawpixel.com/editor_1024/czNmcy1wcml2YXRlL3Jhd3BpeGVsX2ltYWdlcy93ZWJzaXRlX2NvbnRlbnQvbHIvbnMxMDc3Ny1pbWFnZS1rd3Z5ZTMzMS5qcGc.jpg", "credit": "cc0 1.0 · via rawpixel"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 485, "reading_minutes": 1.5, "lead": "黒海でドローンが船を攻撃しました。二つの船が沈み、人が亡くなりました。EUは「ゆるせない」と言いました。", "lead_zh": "黑海发生无人机袭击船只事件。两艘船沉没，有人死亡。欧盟表示“无法接受”。", "preview": "十月六日、ブルガリアの近くの海で、ドローンが二つの貨物船を攻撃しました。トーゴ船籍の「アルファ・ワタン」は沈み、パラオ船籍の「エイブル」は火事になりました。少なくとも二人の船員が亡くなりました。場所はブルガリアの海岸から約八十マイル（百二十八キロ）でした。", "preview_zh": "10月6日，在保加利亚附近海域，无人机袭击了两艘货船。多哥籍的“阿尔法·瓦坦”号沉没，帕劳籍的“埃布尔”号起火。至少两名船员死亡。地点距离保加利亚海岸约80英里（128公里）。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 87, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@9b040a2/content/audio/10/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 101.462, "size_bytes": 612576, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 323, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@9b040a2/content/data/versions/97.json", "paragraphs": ["十月六日、ブルガリアの近くの海で、ドローンが二つの貨物船を攻撃しました。トーゴ船籍の「アルファ・ワタン」は沈み、パラオ船籍の「エイブル」は火事になりました。少なくとも二人の船員が亡くなりました。場所はブルガリアの海岸から約八十マイル（百二十八キロ）でした。", "ブルガリアの首相は「これはゆるせない攻撃だ」と言いました。そして「国際法に反する」とも言いました。「エイブル」の十八人の船員はブルガリアのフェリーに助けられました。二人はけがをして、病院に運ばれました。「アルファ・ワタン」の船員のことはまだ分かっていません。", "その前の日の十月五日にも、ルーマニアの近くの海でドローンがトルコの船「ロヤド・ママドフ」を攻撃しました。この船は火事になって沈みました。十一人は助かりましたが、一人はまだ見つかっていません。二人が亡くなりました。", "EUのフォン・デア・ライエン会長は「ますます心配だ」と言いました。しかし「誰がやったかはまだ分かっていない」とも言いました。ウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は「ロシアの攻撃だ」と言いました。", "この戦争で、黒海の船の攻撃が増えています。ロシアとウクライナはドローンを使っています。EUやNATOの国々は心配しています。インドは「戦いをやめてほしい」と言っています。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["10月6日，在保加利亚附近海域，无人机袭击了两艘货船。多哥籍的“阿尔法·瓦坦”号沉没，帕劳籍的“埃布尔”号起火。至少两名船员死亡。地点距离保加利亚海岸约80英里（128公里）。", "保加利亚总理说：“这是不可接受的攻击。”他还说：“这违反国际法。”“埃布尔”号的18名船员被保加利亚的渡轮救起。两人受伤，被送往医院。“阿尔法·瓦坦”号船员的情况尚不清楚。", "前一天10月5日，在罗马尼亚附近海域，无人机也袭击了土耳其船只“罗亚德·马马多夫”号。这艘船起火后沉没。11人获救，但一人仍失踪。两人死亡。", "欧盟委员会主席冯德莱恩说：“越来越令人担忧。”但她也说：“还不知道是谁干的。”乌克兰总统泽连斯基说：“这是俄罗斯的袭击。”", "这场战争中，黑海船只遭袭事件在增加。俄罗斯和乌克兰都在使用无人机。欧盟和北约国家很担心。印度表示“希望停止战斗”。"], "body": "十月六日、ブルガリアの近くの海で、ドローンが二つの貨物船を攻撃しました。トーゴ船籍の「アルファ・ワタン」は沈み、パラオ船籍の「エイブル」は火事になりました。少なくとも二人の船員が亡くなりました。場所はブルガリアの海岸から約八十マイル（百二十八キロ）でした。\n\nブルガリアの首相は「これはゆるせない攻撃だ」と言いました。そして「国際法に反する」とも言いました。「エイブル」の十八人の船員はブルガリアのフェリーに助けられました。二人はけがをして、病院に運ばれました。「アルファ・ワタン」の船員のことはまだ分かっていません。\n\nその前の日の十月五日にも、ルーマニアの近くの海でドローンがトルコの船「ロヤド・ママドフ」を攻撃しました。この船は火事になって沈みました。十一人は助かりましたが、一人はまだ見つかっていません。二人が亡くなりました。\n\nEUのフォン・デア・ライエン会長は「ますます心配だ」と言いました。しかし「誰がやったかはまだ分かっていない」とも言いました。ウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は「ロシアの攻撃だ」と言いました。\n\nこの戦争で、黒海の船の攻撃が増えています。ロシアとウクライナはドローンを使っています。EUやNATOの国々は心配しています。インドは「戦いをやめてほしい」と言っています。", "body_zh": "10月6日，在保加利亚附近海域，无人机袭击了两艘货船。多哥籍的“阿尔法·瓦坦”号沉没，帕劳籍的“埃布尔”号起火。至少两名船员死亡。地点距离保加利亚海岸约80英里（128公里）。\n\n保加利亚总理说：“这是不可接受的攻击。”他还说：“这违反国际法。”“埃布尔”号的18名船员被保加利亚的渡轮救起。两人受伤，被送往医院。“阿尔法·瓦坦”号船员的情况尚不清楚。\n\n前一天10月5日，在罗马尼亚附近海域，无人机也袭击了土耳其船只“罗亚德·马马多夫”号。这艘船起火后沉没。11人获救，但一人仍失踪。两人死亡。\n\n欧盟委员会主席冯德莱恩说：“越来越令人担忧。”但她也说：“还不知道是谁干的。”乌克兰总统泽连斯基说：“这是俄罗斯的袭击。”\n\n这场战争中，黑海船只遭袭事件在增加。俄罗斯和乌克兰都在使用无人机。欧盟和北约国家很担心。印度表示“希望停止战斗”。", "text": "十月六日、ブルガリアの近くの海で、ドローンが二つの貨物船を攻撃しました。トーゴ船籍の「アルファ・ワタン」は沈み、パラオ船籍の「エイブル」は火事になりました。少なくとも二人の船員が亡くなりました。場所はブルガリアの海岸から約八十マイル（百二十八キロ）でした。 ブルガリアの首相は「これはゆるせない攻撃だ」と言いました。そして「国際法に反する」とも言いました。「エイブル」の十八人の船員はブルガリアのフェリーに助けられました。二人はけがをして、病院に運ばれました。「アルファ・ワタン」の船員のことはまだ分かっていません。 その前の日の十月五日にも、ルーマニアの近くの海でドローンがトルコの船「ロヤド・ママドフ」を攻撃しました。この船は火事になって沈みました。十一人は助かりましたが、一人はまだ見つかっていません。二人が亡くなりました。 EUのフォン・デア・ライエン会長は「ますます心配だ」と言いました。しかし「誰がやったかはまだ分かっていない」とも言いました。ウクライナのゼレンスキー大統領は「ロシアの攻撃だ」と言いました。 この戦争で、黒海の船の攻撃が増えています。ロシアとウクライナはドローンを使っています。EUやNATOの国々は心配しています。インドは「戦いをやめてほしい」と言っています。", "vocab": [{"word": "ドローン", "pos": "noun", "zh": "无人机", "note": "外来语，常用"}, {"word": "貨物船", "pos": "noun", "zh": "货船", "note": "かもつせん"}, {"word": "沈む", "pos": "verb", "zh": "沉没", "note": "しずむ，五段动词"}, {"word": "攻撃", "pos": "noun", "zh": "攻击", "note": "こうげき，也可作动词"}, {"word": "船員", "pos": "noun", "zh": "船员", "note": "せんいん"}, {"word": "亡くなる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "死亡", "note": "なかくなる，委婉说法"}, {"word": "助ける", "pos": "verb", "zh": "救助", "note": "たすける，一段动词"}, {"word": "けが", "pos": "noun", "zh": "受伤", "note": "常用名词"}, {"word": "国際法", "pos": "noun", "zh": "国际法", "note": "こくさいほう"}, {"word": "心配", "pos": "noun", "zh": "担心", "note": "しんぱい，也可作动词"}], "title_original": "Drones sink ships near NATO countries in “unacceptable” attacks, EU says", "summary_original": "Two cargo ships have sunk, one ship was afire, and sailors are dead or missing.", "body_original": "“This business will get out of control”\nDrones sink ships near NATO countries in “unacceptable” attacks, EU says\nTwo cargo ships have sunk, one ship was afire, and sailors are dead or missing.\nJeremy Hsu\n–\nOct 6, 2026 5:31 pm\n|\n49\nA long trail of dark smoke drifts across the horizon from a commercial grain cargo ship struck by a Russian drone attack in the Black Sea off the coast of Odesa, Ukraine, on July 14.\nCredit:\nIuliia Kuzmina / iStock Editorial / Getty Images\nA long trail of dark smoke drifts across the horizon from a commercial grain cargo ship struck by a Russian drone attack in the Black Sea off the coast of Odesa, Ukraine, on July 14.\nCredit:\nIuliia Kuzmina / iStock Editorial / Getty Images\nText\nsettings\nStory text\nSize\nSmall\nStandard\nLarge\nWidth\n*\nStandard\nWide\nLinks\nStandard\nOrange\n* Subscribers only\nLearn more\nMinimize to nav\nDrones sank two cargo ships and damaged a third in the exclusive economic zones of NATO member countries for the first time, killing at least two sailors. The attacks represent a notable escalation as Black Sea commercial shipping has increasingly come under attack during the Russian invasion of Ukraine, with Russia also being accused of carrying out “hybrid warfare” incidents across Europe.\nThe Togo-flagged cargo ship\nAlfa Watan\nsank, and the Palau-flagged cargo ship\nAble\nwas set ablaze after being attacked by multiple sea and aerial drones about 80 miles (128 kilometers) off the coast of Bulgaria on October 6,\naccording to the Associated Press\n. In an interview, Bulgarian Prime Minister Rumen Radev described the incidents as “an unacceptable attack in Bulgaria’s exclusive economic zone” and “a blatant violation of international law and maritime law.”\nThe fate of the\nAlfa Watan’\ns crew was not immediately known after the vessel sank. A Bulgarian ferry managed to evacuate the 18 crew members of the\nAble\n, with two severely injured mariners being flown to a hospital in the city of Varna.\nThis comes one day after drones struck the Turkish-owned cargo ship named\nRoyad Mammadov\nwithin Romania’s exclusive economic zone in the Black Sea on October 5. That ship caught fire and eventually sank, with 11 crew members rescued by Romanian ships and helicopters while one crew member remains missing,\naccording to Euronews\n. Two crew members were killed.\nEuropean Union president Ursula von der Leyen described the drone strikes on the three vessels in the Black Sea as “increasingly concerning” in a\npost on X\n. But she also cautioned that the circumstances of the attacks are “still being established” without naming a probable attacker.\n“Attacks on civilian shipping are unacceptable,” Leyen wrote. “We stand in full solidarity with our Member States on the Eastern flank.”\nBy contrast, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy described a joint investigation with Bulgaria’s navy as finding that the latest strikes represented a “Russian combined attack using both sea and aerial drones,”\nReuters reported\n. Zelenskyy also said that Ukraine’s military was not conducting operations in that part of the Black Sea.\nWidening Black Sea warfare\nThe attacks represent the widening consequences of the ongoing war that escalated sharply with Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. Despite lacking much of a traditional navy, Ukraine has successfully challenged Russian naval control of the Black Sea by deploying both aerial drones and drone boats to strike Russian warships and ports.\nUkrainian drones have also stepped up\nattacks on Russian-linked oil and gas tankers along with other supply ships\n. In a milestone for naval warfare, a\nUkrainian sea drone even used a machine gun to sink a Russian kamikaze drone boat\ncarrying explosives in September 2026.\nBut Russia has also increasingly deployed its own aerial drones and sea drones to attack Ukrainian ships and ports, along with\nattacking international commercial ships\ncarrying\ngrain and other cargo from Ukraine\nor docked in Ukrainian ports.\nThe cargo ship\nAble\nwas carrying wheat and sailing south when the drones attacked, while the\nAlfa Watan\nwas heading north with the cargo being unknown. The\nRoyad Mammadov\nhad been carrying corn loaded in the Ukrainian port of Ismail when it was reportedly attacked by both aerial drones and drone boats.\nIn a\nsocial media post\nreacting to the earlier attack on the\nRoyad Mammadov\n, Zelenskyy condemned the “horrific strike by two Russian drones on a civilian vessel in neutral waters” and reiterated Ukrainian efforts to “de-escalate the situation and ensure security in the Black Sea.”\n“But Russia consistently chooses terror and sinking civilian vessels instead of normal maritime navigation,” Zelenskyy wrote. “Pressure is needed to restore global food security.”\nZelenskyy also referred to “relevant proposals from third countries” on this topic. India has been holding discussions with both Ukraine and Russia on safeguarding shipping in the Black Sea and has generally called for a halt to the fighting,\naccording to Bloomberg News\n.\nIndia has a strategic partnership with Russia that includes the Indian military using Russian fighter jets and air defense systems, while the country continues to purchase Russian oil for its energy needs. But many Indian citizens also work as seafarers on commercial vessels that have come under attack in the Black Sea and Strait of Hormuz, with three Indian nationals having been aboard the\nRoyad Mammadov\nand one\nbeing injured in the attack\n.\nHybrid warfare in Europe\nThe latest drone strikes on ships off the coasts of Romania and Bulgaria coincide with a growing number of incidents attributed to Russian hybrid warfare or gray-zone tactics aimed at multiple European countries within the NATO alliance.\nRussian embassy officials have denied this\n, but the evidence continues to accumulate, with multiple European governments pointing to Russia.\nFor example, Romanian military divers previously\ndestroyed two Russian-made drones found floating in the Black Sea\nnear the vital European natural gas project called Neptun Deep in August. A few weeks later, Romania\nscrambled fighter jets to disable a Russian drone boat\nloaded with explosives that was also discovered near the same offshore gas platform.\nGermany has also\nformally accused Russia\nof organizing an\nattempted explosive drone attack on Ukrainian cargo aircraft\nparked at Leipzig Airport in August. Meanwhile, Estonia has also described Russian special services as being behind an\narson attack on the Estonian company Milrem Robotics\n, which supplies Ukraine with\nmilitary robotic vehicles\n.\nSimilarly, Poland has been investigating a fire at a state-owned satellite station using SpaceX’s\nStarlink communication service\nas an “act of sabotage” that aligns with a “new Russian doctrine of attack,” according to Polish Deputy Prime Minister Krzysztof Gawkowski as\nreported by BBC News\n.\nMuch of the NATO alliance is still rearming and trying to\nadapt to modern warfare dominated by drones\n, which both\nUkraine and Russia have already spent years developing and practicing on the battlefield\n. But the Russian-instigated hybrid warfare across Europe poses a different immediate challenge—can NATO member countries agree on a strategy for discouraging sabotage and other provocative incidents from a nuclear-armed adversary?\nJeremy Hsu\nTech Reporter\nJeremy Hsu\nTech Reporter\nJeremy Hsu is a reporter exploring a wide range of topics across deep tech and AI. He has previously written for New Scientist, Scientific American, IEEE Spectrum, Wired, Undark Magazine and MIT Tech Review, among many other publications, about topics such as deepfakes, data centers, drones, battery tech, robotics, and GPS jamming. He also has a Master of Arts in Journalism from NYU, and a bachelor's degree from University of Pennsylvania in History and Sociology of Science, with a minor in English.\n49 Comments", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:18:30.581254", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "十月", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.675, "sm": 125, "em": 675, "cs": 0, "ce": 2, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "六日", "s": 0.688, "e": 1.113, "sm": 687, "em": 1112, "cs": 2, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "、", "s": 1.113, "e": 1.462, "sm": 1112, "em": 1462, "cs": 4, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "ブルガリア", "s": 1.462, "e": 2.013, "sm": 1462, "em": 2012, "cs": 5, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "の", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.112, "sm": 2025, "em": 2112, "cs": 10, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "近く", "s": 2.125, "e": 2.538, "sm": 2125, "em": 2537, "cs": 11, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "の", "s": 2.55, "e": 2.65, "sm": 2550, "em": 2650, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "海", "s": 2.663, "e": 2.925, "sm": 2662, "em": 2925, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "で", "s": 2.938, "e": 3.112, "sm": 2937, "em": 3112, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "、", "s": 3.112, "e": 3.462, "sm": 3112, "em": 3462, "cs": 16, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "ドローン", "s": 3.462, "e": 3.837, "sm": 3462, "em": 3837, "cs": 17, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "が", "s": 3.85, "e": 3.975, "sm": 3850, "em": 3975, "cs": 21, "ce": 22